      "excerpt": "If a restudy is required because a peer Interconnection Request (IR) withdraws, MISO (the Transmission Provider) will reevaluate and, if necessary, reallocate the cost and responsibility for any Common Use Upgrade and/or Shared Network Upgrade among the remaining Interconnection Customers (ICs). The ICs that remain in the study group may be responsible for funding the restudy and any resulting upgrades, as determined by MISO (BPM-015 r33 §5.4.6). ## Citations - BPM-015 r33 §5",
      "need_search": true
    },
    {
      "question": "Who pays for that, and how many Business Days does the IC have to answer?",
      "response_shape": "short",
      "unit_ids": [
